1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
RegDelta connects regulatory framework changes to client policies and agency actions.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
This prototype uses the public NIST CSF 1.1 to 2.0 transition crosswalk.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:30,000
I’m providing a synthetic client policy. Gemini assesses it against the framework changes.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,000
This run assesses the 12 changes most relevant to the policy. This shortlist does not represent full framework recall.

5
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Each finding includes its rationale and a proposed fix. An unverified quote is not shown as evidence.

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
This is the Bangla action-plan summary for the agency.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
All recommendations are drafts, not final compliance decisions.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The Bangla action plan briefly explains the gaps and suggested work.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Approve, edit, and reject are not yet connected to this workflow, so findings remain drafts for review.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:20,000
GitHub issue creation is not connected yet, and no external action has been taken.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
These are the model and usage details for this live run. All output is for human review.
